msdfgen: walk contours, edges and edge selectors with pointers in the per-pixel loops

ShapeDistanceFinder::distance() and OverlappingContourCombiner::reset() run once per output texel
(and again per error-correction probe). They walked std::vector with iterators. Under the MSVC
debug runtime (_ITERATOR_DEBUG_LEVEL=2) every iterator construction, copy and destruction locks
a global mutex to adopt or orphan the iterator, which made generateMTSDF about 56 s of the 60 s
MSVC Debug budget of text_import.font.latin_metrics_and_determinism (DENG-758). Pointer and index
walks visit the same elements in the same order, so every output bit is unchanged; release
builds compile both forms to the same code.

Engine-local patch (DENG-758), applied by tools/vendor/vendor.py. Drop it if a pinned msdfgen
release stops using iterators in these loops.

